    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may make filters more restrictive without thinking about users**\r\n\r\nSome students may choose thresholds that sound precise but remove too many useful opportunities. Encourage them to think about the user impact by asking: **\"Who can still find opportunities with this filter, and who might be left out?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nif (jobs[i].distance <= 3) {\r\n  results.push(jobs[i]);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students see that changing a filter changes who the app serves.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may not update the button label to match the new rule**\r\n\r\nStudents may change the logic but leave the button text as a generic label like `Distance` or `Experience`. Ask: **\"Would a user know what this filter does before clicking it?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nbtnDistance.textContent = \"Bikeable\";\r\nbtnExperience.textContent = \"Entry-level\";\r\nbtnSchedule.textContent = \"Weekday afternoons\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that filter labels should clearly describe the rule.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may forget to give feedback after filtering**\r\n\r\nSome students will render the filtered results but not update the result message. Encourage them to add transparency by asking: **\"After the filter runs, how does the user know what changed?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nresultCount.textContent =\r\n  \"Showing entry-level opportunities that require 1 year of experience or less. \" +\r\n  results.length +\r\n  \" results found.\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students connect filtering logic to clear user feedback.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may only test whether a filter returns results**\r\n\r\nStudents may click a button, see some jobs, and assume the filter works. Encourage them to inspect the actual data by asking: **\"Do all displayed jobs match the rule you chose?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nif (jobs[i].schedule === \"weekday-afternoon\") {\r\n  results.push(jobs[i]);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that testing a filter means checking both what is included and what is excluded."
  },
